From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] BiosAttributeRegistry: emit schema-shaped Value and bare
 AttributeName

GenerateAttributeDetails() builds each registry entry's allowable values
as "Values": ["A", "B"] - a flat string array under a key that does not
exist in the AttributeRegistry schema. ProvisionAttributeRegistry() then
round-trips the whole document through the v1_3_6 schema converter
(ToStructure -> ToJson) before the PUT, and the converter keeps only what
its generated CS structure models: every scalar survives, the one
off-schema array vanishes. Observed on hardware: all 13 enumeration
attributes reached the BMC with Type "Enumeration" but no value list at
all, so no client could learn what a setting accepts.

Emit what DSP2046 actually defines - "Value", an array of AttributeValue
objects ({"ValueName", "ValueDisplayName"}), which the converter CS does
model (RedfishAttributeRegistry_V1_3_6_AttributeValue_Array_CS) and
therefore preserves.

While in the same function: AttributeName was the raw configure language
("/Bios/Attributes/FanMode"), not the key the Bios resource serves under
Attributes ("FanMode"). RedfishPlatformConfigGetAttribute already derives
the bare name from the x-UEFI string; use it, falling back to the raw key
only when it is absent, so registry entries correlate with attributes the
way the schema intends.

Upstream-Status: Submittable [matches DSP2046; converter already models it]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/RedfishClientPkg/Features/BiosAttributeRegistry/Common/BiosAttributeRegistryCommon.c
+++ b/RedfishClientPkg/Features/BiosAttributeRegistry/Common/BiosAttributeRegistryCommon.c
@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@
 {
   EDKII_JSON_VALUE         AttributeValue;
   EDKII_JSON_VALUE         AttributeArray;
+  EDKII_JSON_VALUE         ValueObj;
   EFI_STATUS               Status;
   EDKII_REDFISH_ATTRIBUTE  Attribute;
   EDKII_REDFISH_VALUE      DefaultValue;
@@ -251,9 +252,18 @@
 
   //
   // Create required attributes for BMC
-  // AttributeName
+  // AttributeName. Use the terminal segment of the configure language
+  // (already derived by RedfishPlatformConfigGetAttribute) so the entry
+  // carries the same key the Bios resource serves under Attributes, per
+  // DSP2046 -- the full configure-language path is not a valid
+  // AttributeName and clients cannot correlate it.
   //
-  AttributeValue = JsonValueInitAsciiString (Key);
+  if (Attribute.AttributeName != NULL) {
+    AttributeValue = JsonValueInitAsciiString (Attribute.AttributeName);
+  } else {
+    AttributeValue = JsonValueInitAsciiString (Key);
+  }
+
   if (AttributeValue == NULL) {
     Status = EFI_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
     goto RELEASE;
@@ -424,17 +434,34 @@
   }
 
   //
-  // Values
+  // Value. DSP2046 models the possible values as an array of
+  // AttributeValue objects under "Value"; the flat "Values" string array
+  // this used to emit is not in the AttributeRegistry schema, so the
+  // ToStructure/ToJson round-trip in ProvisionAttributeRegistry silently
+  // dropped it and no enumeration ever reached the BMC.
   //
   if ((Attribute.Type == RedfishAttributeTypeEnumeration) && (Attribute.Values.ValueCount > 0)) {
     AttributeArray = JsonValueInitArray ();
 
     for (Index = 0; Index < Attribute.Values.ValueCount; Index++) {
-      AttributeValue = JsonValueInitAsciiString (Attribute.Values.ValueArray[Index].ValueName);
-      JsonArrayAppendValue (AttributeArray, AttributeValue);
+      if (Attribute.Values.ValueArray[Index].ValueName == NULL) {
+        continue;
+      }
+
+      ValueObj = JsonValueInitObject ();
+      if (ValueObj == NULL) {
+        continue;
+      }
+
+      JsonObjectSetValue (ValueObj, "ValueName", JsonValueInitAsciiString (Attribute.Values.ValueArray[Index].ValueName));
+      if (Attribute.Values.ValueArray[Index].ValueDisplayName != NULL) {
+        JsonObjectSetValue (ValueObj, "ValueDisplayName", JsonValueInitAsciiString (Attribute.Values.ValueArray[Index].ValueDisplayName));
+      }
+
+      JsonArrayAppendValue (AttributeArray, ValueObj);
     }
 
-    JsonObjectSetValue (*AttributeObj, "Values", AttributeArray);
+    JsonObjectSetValue (*AttributeObj, "Value", AttributeArray);
   }
 
   Status = EFI_SUCCESS;
